ed_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lordrenar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lordrenar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lordrenar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lordrenar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lordrenar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lordrenar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T09:37:16Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T09:57:47Z","body":"update. @Nodragem I've tested the error, and i'm pretty sure it happens:\n1. First time i load godot editor and i run the game, expecially if i switch window focus while it's loading the game\n2. If something needs to be saved between the \"run the game\" and the game is loaded, expecially if you switch focus of the window. The problem arise if, for example, i run the game after i've modify something in the core scene of the level, first thing godot saves the scene, then runs the game, there we have the error.\nAnother example if you save something in runtime ( i save a dictionary of things ).\n\nThe first case it's probably connected to the second, first time the editor runs the game it probably saves something.\nCan you test if you can reproduce the problem ? It's driving me crazy\n\nbtw running 4.6.2, but that's not the issue i think\n\nIf you can reproduce the error with the steps above, it's a good step in finding a way to find the bugged shaders","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4496834991/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5279045535","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119384#issuecomment-5279045535","issue_url"